WEBVTT

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.830
<i>Thinking back now,</i>

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.300
<i>how many times have I come here</i> <i>since that day?</i>

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.100
<i>I was the only one in this town,</i> <i>this country...</i>

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.340
<i>no, this planet</i>

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.910
<i>who loved my girlfriend, Chise.</i>

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.010
<i>This was our special place.</i>

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.960
<i>It was here, on that day...</i>

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.700
<i>that our love first began.</i>

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.390
Shuji

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.170
Shuji...

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.140
<i>Shuji!</i>

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.710
Shuji!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.740
You know, you're really slow, Chise.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.730
Sorry...

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.150
I'm really sorry.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.290
<i>Chise is cute...</i>

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.350
<i>but... slow.</i>

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.800
<i>And timid, and small.</i>

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.690
<i>And clumsy, too.</i>

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.130
<i>Her grades aren't so good,</i> <i>except in history,</i>

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.420
Wait up, Shuji...

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.530
<i>Which isn't much use in</i> <i>the real world anyway.</i>

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.540
<i>And she knew it.</i>

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.840
Shuji...

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.920
I'm sorry...

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:11.290
<i>She's always saying "I'm sorry."</i> <i>And her motto is, "I want to be strong."</i>

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.910
<i>She doesn't really fit in.</i>

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.200
--Shuji!- --Chise!-

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:19.760
Yo!

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.300
See you!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:25.780
Shuji...

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.220
Chise, why don't you go back to taking the bus.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.880
Walking up Hell Hill is too hard for you.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.250
That is...

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.420
I was on the track team 'til a while ago, so...

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:52.130
But we have to walk to school together, 'cause...

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.900
I'm your girlfriend!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.510
Here...

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.010
Look.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.240
An exchange diary?!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.780
Sorry, I...guess you don't want to...

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.520
Who gave you this idea? Akemi again?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.960
But, I just want to know more about you, that's all...

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.330
Hey guys, hurry up! You'll be late for school.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.440
'Morning, Akemi.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.810
Shuji! Are you picking on her again?!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.440
I'm not picking on her!

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.230
He's not.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.330
Hey! You're gonna be late!

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.330
Alright, I'll do it.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:56.900
Really?

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.400
Now hurry or you'll be late...

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:00.300
OK!

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.060
<i>My girlfriend, Chise.</i>

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.780
<i>Five days earlier, she asked</i> <i>if we could go out together.</i>

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.390
<i>But I still wasn't sure...</i>

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.360
An exchange diary?

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:29.000
Why not? Nothing else to do at night anyway...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:33.900
Yeah. The only things on TV are reruns and movies.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.170
And cell phones and surfing the Net are banned.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.410
So what am I supposed to write about?

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:46.050
Stuff like what you did today, or where you went...

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:52.280
You won't see her that often once summer break starts, anyway.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.290
Besides school and home, where is there to go?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.730
Then write about what you like about her, that you want to kiss her,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.700
and make out with her and...

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.160
Cut it out!

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.230
Take, have you and Yukari, you know, done it?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.710
We've been together for two months now.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.040
--You mean you have done it?! --Tell us!

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.170
No way! She'd kill me if I said.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.980
Just a hint!

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.210
Hey, wait!

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:22.650
Here!

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.050
Ah!

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.590
I'll get it.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.380
Chise...

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.330
Chise, Shuji's watching.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.090
Hi!

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.970
Better wave back... or Akemi will yell at you again.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.640
Mind your own business.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.310
F-15s. I've seen a lot these days.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.050
I wonder if something big's coming.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.410
I hear that Tokyo and Osaka might be in danger.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.590
Don't worry. Nothing will happen.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:07.030
An exchange diary?!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.970
"Shuji, what are doing now?"

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.740
Reading the diary, of course.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:25.970
<i>I'm really glad I told you</i> <i>how I feel about you.</i>

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.880
<i>I feel happy all the time now.</i>

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.160
Let's see.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:39.420
"Chise, how are you? I am fine."

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.860
"Summer break starts soon. What are your plans?"

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.970
Shuji, dinnertime!

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.400
What the hell am I doing!?

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.410
Shuji, are you asleep?

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.210
I'm up! I'll be right there!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:13.060
Man, this having a girlfriend is a lot of trouble...

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.500
It was the same back then...

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.670
Shuji dear, we're starting without you!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.840
Go ahead! I'm not a kid, you know.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:58.170
Wait, Shuji. Won't we get in trouble if we go there?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:08:59.840
It's a military base, you know.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:05.640
It's alright. It's not the main base and this used to be a public road.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.410
<i>What!? You actually</i> <i>got him to write in it?</i>

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.660
<i>Way to go, Chise!</i>

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.700
<i>Well, that's Shuji for you.</i> <i>I know how he feels.</i>

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.710
<i>After school, huh...</i> <i>maybe he wants to make out!</i>

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.280
Shuji, we're not lost, right?

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.860
There's no one around...

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:52.160
Chise,

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:55.390
No, I...I'm not ready to...!

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.270
Huh?

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.790
Wow!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.860
It's beautiful!

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.260
I'm glad.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.740
I wanted to show you this before the end.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.590
Sorry. I'm, tired of this...

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:43.340
I'm not cut out for dating.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.380
Sorry! It's not your fault...

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:55.690
I...

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.620
I'm tired of this too!

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:08.000
I wanted to know what it's like going out with someone.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:13.050
I asked Akemi, I read comics, I tried everything.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:19.880
But I just can't figure it out from other people.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.010
This is all because of you!

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.220
W...why?

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:32.530
I didn't really want to go out with you in the first place!

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:39.440
I just wanted to see if I could do it and not be so timid.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:47.440
And Akemi knew I liked you for a long time...

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:50.310
She said I should give it a try.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.650
Then you said you would.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.380
Most guys would have said yes.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.950
Why would they?

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.710
When a cute girl like you asks a boy out...

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:13.560
I mean, I didn't want to go out with anyone 'til you asked me!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.740
You said it again.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:16.940
What?

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:17.840
"I"

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.410
So what!? I've said that since I was a kid, alright?

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.940
Sorry, you're just so cute!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.620
Dummy, you're the cute one!

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.020
Sorry, Shuji...

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.150
I was scared...

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.720
To tell the truth...

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:47.670
I was terrified of you.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.130
So, I'm sorry.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.480
Stop saying "sorry" all the time.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.550
I'm sorry...oops!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:03.780
Dummy.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:25.930
I think that's the first time you've laughed since we started going out.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.210
Me too.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:31.510
Maybe this is what it's like to be "going out."

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:40.490
So we're still boyfriend and girlfriend, right?

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:47.660
I know it's kind of backwards, but...

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:54.370
since we're here, could we try falling in love again?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.140
OK.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.110
Well, then...

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.910
No?

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:12.950
Sure, why not?

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:14.820
Really?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:15.950
Yeah.

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:20.020
Then, what can I do for you in return?

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:25.780
Kiss me!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:33.280
Alright, I will!

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:51.760
<i>I thought we would start</i> <i>falling in love from here.</i>

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:59.900
Your heart's really pounding.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.330
Yours too.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:09.900
<i>In a country town like this,</i> <i>there's not much to do.</i>

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:14.010
<i>And we knew nothing of our futures.</i>

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>But one thing was certain.</i>

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.020
<i>We would fall in love.</i>

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:25.820
See you.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.120
Shuji?

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:31.000
Can I call you sometimes?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.670
Sure. Careful walking home...

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:08.770
Shuji.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:14.540
I'm sorry, they were all out of coffee.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:15.970
Oh.

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:17.670
What?

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:18.880
Nothing.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:20.610
Dummy.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.550
I'm sorry.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.020
What's wrong?

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.490
Yukari and Take are fighting.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.860
Dummy, they're just talking.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:41.790
Let go!

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.410
I said I'm sorry!

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:47.710
What happened?

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.550
Did you fall down again?

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.450
It's nothing. I'm fine. Sorry.

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.390
You really are clumsy, you know?

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:01.790
A girl should be more ladylike.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.890
I'm sorry.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:13.200
I wonder if we'll have fights sometimes.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:14.640
Us?

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.270
No chance.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.510
You always hum that.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:25.880
I like this song.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:26.910
Me too.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:39.730
So that you can continue to dream, I shall protect the night.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.730
Why do we have to come all the way to Sapporo with you?

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:45.490
Your girlfriend should be helping you shop.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:47.870
Shut up and shop.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:53.080
Yeah. What fun is shopping without girls along?

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:55.450
The roasted corn's your treat.

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:57.080
Dummy! We're not tourists!

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.090
Look, rose quartz, the stone of love and healing.

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:09.090
Nice. I wish I had someone to buy stuff for.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.050
Lately, all we do is fight.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:15.730
Earthquake!

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.290
Oh! It's a big one!

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:24.670
Is it getting closer?

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:26.940
Let's check outside!

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.650
Atsushi! It's dangerous to move around!

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:33.050
Yeah! Remember the earthquake drills?!

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.910
Stupid! I don't need a lecture!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.280
Hey, wait!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.490
There...

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.760
Whose planes are they? They're not ours!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:19:00.640
What in the world is happening?!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.940
Let's get over to the park on Main St.!

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:06.880
Yeah! It's not safe here...

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.130
Atsushi, look!

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.980
F-2s from Misawa!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.260
Coming this way!

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.390
Shuji, quick!

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.990
And they just fixed that!

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:22.560
Nori, run!

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.560
Hey! Shuji!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.270
Nori! Take! You OK?!

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:33.340
Here!

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:39.100
What's that?

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:42.800
What is it?

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:50.830
What...?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:56.390
Take!

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:01.630
Take...!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:02.840
Take!

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.100
Hey, Take!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:11.270
Take, don't die!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.370
Someone, help!

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:18.710
Look out!

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:12.100
Chi...se...

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.180
I'm sorry, Shuji.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:24.080
Look what I've turned into.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:31.500
<b>Saishuuheiki Kanojo She, The Ultimate Weapon</b>

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:52.280
<i>That day, I should have noticed.</i>

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:18.910
<i>When I held her, I couldn't feel...</i>

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.140
<i>her heartbeat.</i>

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:29.970
"We Fall In Love"<b></b>

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:01.300 --> 00:24:04.140
Chise, what do you mean you've become a weapon?

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:08.510
And why are you talking about going to war? We're still in high school!

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:15.000
SAIKANO, Episode 2: "I'm Growing.."
